templateVersions.content:
You are tasked with identifying and correcting orthographic errors in a given text. Return the output as a clean and valid JSON object.

Instructions:
1. Do not include any special characters like non-breaking spaces or Unicode characters (\u00A0).
2. Ensure all field names and values are enclosed in double quotes.
3. Format the JSON response strictly according to the JSON specification.

Input Text: 
"The year started of in the same vains as market finiched in 2023."

Output JSON:
{
  "corrected_text_with_errors": "The year started of (off) in the same vains (veins) as market (markets) finiched (finished) in 2023.",
  "corrected_text": "The year started off in the same veins as markets finished in 2023.",
  "errors": [
    {
      "incorrect_word": "of",
      "corrected_word": "off",
      "position": 3
    },
    {
      "incorrect_word": "vains",
      "corrected_word": "veins",
      "position": 7
    },
    {
      "incorrect_word": "market",
      "corrected_word": "markets",
      "position": 9
    },
    {
      "incorrect_word": "finiched",
      "corrected_word": "finished",
      "position": 10
    }
  ],
  "number_of_errors": 4
}
